# One rule for every platform: text is LF in the repo AND in the working tree,
# whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows ships autocrlf=true, which
# otherwise checks files out as CRLF and leaves the index thinking they are clean.
# Published JSON is hashed byte-for-byte (discDigests) and served verbatim by
# Pages, so a CRLF copy no longer matches its digest.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.bin binary
*.mim binary
